["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RequirementStatusType/retired", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A requirement is no longer active for a specific use.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/eori", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[Economic Operators Registration and Identification (EORI) number](https://taxation-customs.ec.europa.eu/customs/customs-procedures-import-and-export/customs-operations/economic-operators-registration-and-identification-number-eori_en) is a unique identifier for businesses undertaking customs operations across European Union customs territory, such as import, export, and transit. It consists of an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code followed by a national identifier of up to 15 alphanumeric characters (e.g., `PL1234567890ABCDE`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N0ee680a8781545b4a492d8ed9169b8c7", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#maxCount", "1", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SbomType/analyzed", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "SBOM generated through analysis of artifacts (e.g., executables, packages, containers, and virtual machine images) after its build. Such analysis generally requires a variety of heuristics. In some contexts, this may also be referred to as a \"3rd party\" SBOM.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/statusNotes", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty", "globalId", "", ""]
